{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["<b>And the garment.</b> Rabbi Yossi the Galilean says: this teaches about garments that they require banishment outside the three camps." "<b>In a garment of wool or in a garment of linen.</b> Regarding garments, it placed wool before linen, because a woolen garment, once its manufacture is completed, is more valuable than a linen garment. But for warp and weft, it placed linen before wool, because linen thread is more valuable than that of wool."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:57.307408264Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}